\f0\fs24 \cf0 DB Schema:\
Table: geozones\
  id, name, type: 'allowed'|'restricted'|'speed'|'curfew'|'poi'|'corridor'|'custom'\
  shapeType: 'polygon'|'circle'|'corridor'\
  coordinates: JSON (GeoJSON polygon or \{lat,lng,radius\} for circle)\
  \
  // Rules\
  alertOnEntry: boolean\
  alertOnExit: boolean\
  speedLimitKph: number (nullable)\
  maxDwellMinutes: number (nullable)\
  curfewStart: string HH:MM (nullable)\
  curfewEnd: string HH:MM (nullable)\
  \
  // Assignments\
  assignedTo: 'all'|'fleet'|'vehicle'|'driver'\
  assignedIds: string[]\
  \
  // Links\
  poiId: FK \uc0\u8594  poi.id (nullable)\
  routeId: FK \uc0\u8594  routes.id (nullable \'97 corridor zones)\
  \
  active: boolean\
  color: string (hex)\
  createdBy: userId FK\
  createdAt, updatedAt\
\
API:\
GET    /api/fleetpoint/geozones              \'97 list all\
GET    /api/fleetpoint/geozones/:id          \'97 single\
GET    /api/fleetpoint/geozones/:id/analytics \'97 visits, dwell, violations\
GET    /api/fleetpoint/geozones/active       \'97 zones with vehicles inside RIGHT NOW\
POST   /api/fleetpoint/geozones              \'97 create (GeoJSON body)\
PATCH  /api/fleetpoint/geozones/:id          \'97 update\
DELETE /api/fleetpoint/geozones/:id          \'97 delete\
\
Geofence checking (backend):\
On every GPS ping \uc0\u8594  check if vehicle is inside/outside any active geozone\
Use PostGIS ST_Within() for efficient polygon containment check\
On state change (inside\uc0\u8594 outside or outside\u8594 inside):\
  \uc0\u8594  Create geozone_event record\
  \uc0\u8594  If zone.alertOnEntry and entering \u8594  fire alert\
  \uc0\u8594  If zone.alertOnExit and exiting \u8594  fire alert\
  \uc0\u8594  If restricted and entering \u8594  create violation\
  \uc0\u8594  Emit WebSocket event to frontend\
TODO: PostGIS extension required on PostgreSQL\
TODO: Index geozones with ST_MakeEnvelope for performance\
\
Draw on map:\
Use Leaflet.draw plugin for polygon/circle/corridor drawing\
On shape complete \uc0\u8594  extract GeoJSON coordinates\
Store as JSONB in coordinates column}